  "description": "JOKFIB crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H56 Gd4 N12 O16,4(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.887-3.899 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 108.61-114.93°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C64H72Gd4N12O20.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
